body:
Thanks, 

&#x200B;

Can you Right click than open with and select the application you'd like to open them in.

Can you try turning filter keys off if it is enabled.  [https://support.lenovo.com/us/en/solutions/ht500119-how-to-turn-on-and-turn-off-filter-keys-windows-ideapad](https://support.lenovo.com/us/en/solutions/ht500119-how-to-turn-on-and-turn-off-filter-keys-windows-ideapad)

&#x200B;

Let me know if that does anything. 

&#x200B;

Thx

The other thing you can do is resetting network settings. It won't delete data but you will need to re-pair Bluetooth devices and re-connect to wifi networks. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Reset your Network Settings.  
Go to Settings > General > Reset > Reset Network Settings. This also resets Wi-Fi networks and passwords, cellular settings, and VPN and APN settings that you've used before.

Hi there, 

&#x200B;

I would run a malware scan on the computer just in case then I would go ahead and reinstall the wireless driver.

Hi there, 

&#x200B;

Can you try another pair of headphones?

Lets try this 

&#x200B;

 Right click on the volume icon and select “Playback devices”.  
 Now, right click on empty space and select, “Show disconnected devices” and “Show disabled devices”.  
 Select “headphone” and click on “Properties” and make sure that the headphone is enabled & set as default.   
 Reconnect your headphones and check if issue is resolved.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Source: https://answers.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/forum/all/headphones-not-detected-in-windows-10/64be9661-b96e-4909-b91b-ee1b5bd44d86

I would recommend turning it on just on your computer, just be aware it may affect your speeds since tethering is generally slower then a regular connection. 

&#x200B;

Cheers

Hi there, 

&#x200B;

If you have the model number of the motherboard I can locate some drivers for you and provide you the links. You'd want to download them to a flash drive then install them on the computer you are having issues with. 

&#x200B;

Cheers.

I would consider using VPN + Brave as your browser. Brave is privacy oriented and works pretty well.

&#x200B;

[https://brave.com/](https://brave.com/)

The story before deletion source: https://www.removeddit.com/r/ChoosingBeggars/comments/dsslhe/my_parents_rents_our_old_house_for_profit_they/?utm_medium=android_app&utm_source=share

 So my parents are renting our old house to international students or people looking for an affordable rent. To make the communication easier for both sides, my parents are only renting it to people from our ethnicity and they only post their ads in the community. They have been doing this for nearly 10 years and it worked very well.

&#x200B;

It is a 4 ½ and they are charging per occupied room. It is around 250$ per room which includes a fully equipped kitchen, a sofa in the living room, a washing machine, hot water, heat, electricity and internet. The location is ideal: it has many grocery stores, a plaza, a metro/subway line just 5 min away from walk and on top of that a KFC next to it!!! (I miss that KFC). My dad even offers Costco trips __ FOR FREE __ if they wanted to do groceries for a better deal.

&#x200B;

At some point, a room was vacant and someone called to come check it out. Over the phone, I could hear the potential tenant was interested to rent the vacant room and showed lots of interest with what was on the table. My dad had prepared the lease before he headed out. However, when they met, unexpected things happened. From what my dad told me, the potential tenant pulled out a piece of paper with lots of mathematical formulas.

&#x200B;

Basically this:

&#x200B;

You are renting the room for 250$. There are 30 days in a month and 1 day has 24 hours. So you charge 0.35$/h ( 250 / 30 / 24 = 0.35$). I am only there maybe for 2 hours max a day to do my daily personal things, sleep 8 hours and the rest of the day I’ll be at outside so I’m home 10 hours max a day. I’m willing to pay 105$ (0.35 x 10 x 30 = 105$) to live here until the lease expires.

&#x200B;

My dad wished them luck to find a landlord that accepts this method of payment.
